 ],
 "notes": [
  "On 1h, RSI(7) crossing up through MFI(14) gave 16,732 entries in 1,397 separate moves. Twenty candles later those entries were 0.01% behind random ones, inside the luck band. Requiring both lines below 40 keeps roughly a quarter of the crosses, and the result still lands inside the band. Read as a short, the cross down shows nothing on 1h, 4h or daily either.",
  "Going long while RSI(7) stayed above MFI(14) on 1h beat random entries by 0.04%, just past the luck band. SOL carries the result, while BTC and ETH sit inside their bands. The gap comes from 760 entries between Feb 4 and Apr 3, 2021, and it disappears without them. At 10, 50 and 100 candles it shows nothing, and the uptrend and downtrend halves are each inside the band. On daily the same condition forms only 18 separate moves, too few to judge.",
  "Shorting a cross down with both lines above 60 on daily did 6.29% worse than random after 20 days. On SOL alone it did 11.94% worse. Both results rest on 7 entries between Aug 1 and Sep 9, 2021, and without them the result is chance. It also shows at 10 candles but not at 50 or 100. Split by trend, the uptrend and downtrend halves are each inside the luck band.",
  "Two trend splits leave the band, and each rests on one stretch. On 1h, the cross up did 0.05% worse than random in uptrends, from 92 entries between May 21 and Jun 20, 2021. In downtrends it showed nothing. On 4h, the cross up with both lines below 40 did 0.61% worse in downtrends, from 5 entries on Nov 8-13, 2022, during the FTX collapse. In uptrends it showed nothing.",
  "Elsewhere, splitting by trend flips the sign without leaving the band. In uptrends, the 4h short on a cross down was 0.12% behind random, and in downtrends it was 0.13% ahead. The daily cross up was 0.45% ahead in uptrends and 0.11% behind in downtrends. The 1h and 4h shorts from above 60, RSI(7) above MFI(14) on 4h and the daily cross down flip the same way, inside the band each time. The daily cross up from below 40 has too few uptrend moves to judge. The same goes for RSI(7) above MFI(14) on daily in uptrends, while its downtrend half is inside the band.",
  "For a long DCA bot, none of these crossovers improves entry timing on these pairs, so the DCA orders and the take profit do the work. If you keep the cross as a start condition, treat it as a frequent trigger. On 1h it fires about four times as often as on 4h. Use it beside a condition that carries information of its own, or leave it out. It fails in a strong one-way run: the daily short from above 60 lost most of its ground on 7 SOL entries in one stretch."
 ],
